Patch 2054: the texture-slot scan starts at the slot last seen holding the texture (TEX_HINT=0 off).

vp_upload_tex_slot scanned up to 1024 slots on every bind (9% of the drawing thread in v15's Hidden Leaf profile). A
key lives in one slot only, and the free-slot choice is only used when nothing matches, so a remembered slot that still
holds the key is the slot the scan would find. A 4096-entry hash (key, size, format, cube, pitch) remembers it. Ported
from the v15 backend (CPU_PROFILE sec 32).

Tested together (US disc, bench.ps1, same build, A/B alternating, switches 1004/0006/2054 on vs off): demo 26.67 / 27.22 vs 24.02 / 22.62 flips/s, Free Battle 25.10 / 28.98 vs 23.72 / 22.87; the flip-to-done time per frame fell from 13.8-17.7 ms to 7.9-9.5 ms (bench\exp\2026-11-07_2235-v15on1 .. 2339-v15off2).

